ithub.com/ernzo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ernzo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ernzo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ernzo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ernzo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ernzo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ernzo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ernzo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ernzo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ernzo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-11T10:39:17Z","updated_at":"2026-02-15T08:08:35Z","body":"Zero problems in Debian trixie with AMD RX6600..\n\nGodot v4.6.1.rc - Debian GNU/Linux 13 (trixie) on Wayland - Wayland display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated AMD Radeon RX 6600 (RADV NAVI23) - AMD FX(tm)-8350 Eight-Core Processor (8 threads) - 32 GiB memory\n\nAlso works perfectly in 4.6 Stable,\nalbeit I use custom build Editor..\n\n-Could it be related to using X11 (or XWayland) in a Wayland based session?\n\nZorin OS 18 on Wayland - X11 display driver\nvs\nGNU/Linux 13 (trixie) on Wayland - Wayland display driver\n\n-Could it be related to driver version?\n\nThis is what I have:\n```\nlspci -nnk | grep -A3 -E \"VGA|Display\"\n\n03:00.0 VGA compatible controller [0300]: Advanced Micro Devices, Inc. [AMD/ATI] Navi 23 [Radeon RX 6600/6600 XT/6600M] [1002:73ff] (rev c7)\n        Subsystem: Sapphire Technology Limited Device [1da2:e451]\n        Kernel driver in use: amdgpu\n        Kernel modules: amdgpu\n\nglxinfo | grep \"Radeon\"\n\nDevice: AMD Radeon RX 6600 (radeonsi, navi23, LLVM 19.1.7, DRM 3.64, 6.18.10-rt-x64v2-xanmod1) (0x73ff)\nOpenGL renderer string: AMD Radeon RX 6600 (radeonsi, navi23, LLVM 19.1.7, DRM 3.64, 6.18.10-rt-x64v2-xanmod1)\n\n\nglxinfo | grep \"OpenGL\"\n\nOpenGL vendor string: AMD\nOpenGL renderer string: AMD Radeon RX 6600 (radeonsi, navi23, LLVM 19.1.7, DRM 3.64, 6.18.10-rt-x64v2-xanmod1)\nOpenGL core profile version string: 4.6 (Core Profile) Mesa 25.0.7-2\nOpenGL core profile shading language version string: 4.60\nOpenGL core profile context flags: (none)\nOpenGL core profile profile mask: core profile\nOpenGL core profile extensions:\nOpenGL version string: 4.6 (Compatibility Profile) Mesa 25.0.7-2\nOpenGL shading language version string: 4.60\nOpenGL context flags: (none)\nOpenGL profile mask: compatibility profile\nOpenGL extensions:\nOpenGL ES profile version string: OpenGL ES 3.2 Mesa 25.0.7-2\nOpenGL ES profile shading language version string: OpenGL ES GLSL ES 3.20\nOpenGL ES profile extensions:\n\n\nvulkaninfo | grep -i version\n\nVulkan Instance Version: 1.4.309\nVK_LAYER_INTEL_nullhw (INTEL NULL HW) Vulkan version 1.1.73, layer version 1:\nVK_LAYER_MESA_device_select (Linux device selection layer) Vulkan version 1.4.303, layer version 1:\nVK_LAYER_MESA_overlay (Mesa Overlay layer) Vulkan version 1.4.303, layer version 1:\n        apiVersion        = 1.4.305 (4210993)\n        driverVersion     = 25.0.7 (104857607)\n        shaderBinaryVersion  = 1\n        conformanceVersion:\n        VK_KHR_sampler_ycbcr_conversion               : extension revision 14\n        samplerYcbcrConversion             = true\n        apiVersion        = 1.4.305 (4210993)\n        driverVersion     = 0.0.1 (1)\n        shaderBinaryVersion  = 1\n        conformanceVersion:\n        VK_KHR_sampler_ycbcr_conversion                    : extension revision 14\n        samplerYcbcrConversion             = true\n\nmodinfo amdgpu | grep -E \"version|filename\"\n\nfilename:       /lib/modules/6.18.10-rt-x64v2-xanmod1/kernel/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu.ko\nsrcversion:     0C7E02EAF8CFDE5E15BEC5B\nparm:           hws_gws_support:Assume MEC2 FW supports GWS barriers (false = rely on FW version check (Default), true = force supported) (bool)\n\n```\n\nThe driver version I'm using comes from Xanmod Kernel itself, (I guess..)\nit may not be the latest version, but works perfectly here!","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3883608188/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3961010742","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116148#issuecomment-3961010742","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116148","id":3961010742,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7sGDo2","user":{"login":"problem-18-dev","id":253351648,"node_id":"U_kgDODxnW4A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/253351648?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/problem-18-dev","html_url":"https://github.com/problem-18-dev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/problem-18-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/problem-18-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/problem-18-dev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/problem-18-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/problem-18-dev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/problem-18-dev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/problem-18-dev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/problem-18-dev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/problem-18-dev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-25T17:59:49Z","updated_at":"2026-02-25T17:59:49Z","body":"Small update for information:\nIssue is still active on 4.6.1.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues